# ctrlc.script -- PROC06: Ctrl-C 5 s after CTRLCPAR's launch (tools/inject-arm.py launch:CTRLCPAR): by then CTRLCPAR has Pexec'd
# C:\PTERMCH.NCP "c", which waits in Cconin. IKBD make/break: Ctrl 0x1D, C 0x2E, C break 0xAE, Ctrl break 0x9D (kernel/src/ikbd.rs folds
# Ctrl + letter to the control code, Ctrl-C = 0x03). Should the key arrive while the child is still in its Cconws, the output-side break
# (conbrk) terminates it with the same -32.
1000 0x1D
1005 0x2E
1010 0xAE
1015 0x9D
